1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,380
The guys at this level are so easy to intimidate.

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:10,600
I don't have to do anything except show my face.

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:12,460
Yoshitsune!

4
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:16,300
Don't tell me not to want to be like you.

5
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,320
Because, uh...

6
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,100
Because I'm in love with the way you play.

7
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:20,900
Oh, my.

8
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:23,240
It doesn't matter what path I'm on or whatever.

9
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:28,440
Little Mopped Aoi, I'm going to let you in on a little secret, okay?

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,580
There's only one player I've seen in my entire career

11
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:34,040
that may have made me feel the slightest bit jealous.

12
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:35,460
Literally that much.

13
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:37,320
Him? Jealous?

14
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,360
There's no way!

15
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:41,820
Who was it?

16
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:45,300
Old spiky head Kuribayashi.

17
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,760
And you sort of play like him, you know?

18
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:49,880
So being like me isn't going to help you.

19
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:53,000
What? Kuribayashi?

20
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:56,860
Okay, awkward, but, dude, for the past month or so,

21
00:00:56,860 --> 00:01:00,060
I've been watching old videos of his games to steal all his moves.

22
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:01,720
That was a pretty good call.

23
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:03,460
Whatever you're doing, it's working.

24
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:06,820
I know that I can outscore anyone most of the time.

25
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:09,740
However, I'm just one player out of 11.

26
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:12,160
It's not like that for Kuribayashi, though.

27
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:14,080
Man, he makes my guts churn.

28
00:01:16,140 --> 00:01:17,640
And you remind me of him.

29
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,340
But with curly hair, so that's why.

30
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:22,960
I am a little bit jealous of you, too.

31
00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:24,300
Like, the slightest bit.

32
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:25,660
That's insane.

33
00:01:26,660 --> 00:01:28,980
Jealous of me when he plays like that?

34
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:30,140
But that kind of helps.

35
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,900
You saying you're in love with my game is pretty awesome.

36
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,900
I'll sign an autograph for you later.

37
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:36,700
Thanks, Mophead!

38
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:38,040
Ugh.

39
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:38,140
Ugh.

40
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:15,720
It should be an easy enough win if they can just get the ball to Yoshitsune again in the

41
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:22,300
second half, right? That all depends. It's hard to say. Their opponents could surround Yoshitsune

42
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:27,660
and force the others to take the ball, and none of them are playing well today. Not an ideal

43
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:33,800
situation when up against a strong Tokyo Metropolis League team. Also, relying so much

44
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:38,460
on one player wouldn't be smart. I hope they know that and adjust their tactics in the next half.

45
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:45,640
Yoshitsune is a temporary player. They need to try scoring without counting on him. That

46
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:47,180
would benefit the team overall.

47
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:50,800
Makes sense.

48
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,740
Whoa, what's wrong?

49
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:58,700
My knees just straight up cave out. It's wild that such a fierce player would be giving himself

50
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,380
a tune-up on the B team, you know?

51
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:05,380
Right! So take lots of pictures, okay? That's gonna be an awesome article!

52
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:12,760
Hana, when it comes to soccer, you really don't know much, do you?

53
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:26,820
Are we all clear? Nothing changes. Just get that ball to Yoshitsune. We can't have a

54
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:30,340
fifth consecutive loss, so suck it up and let him be the star.

55
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:33,980
What are you, Bobby Robson? Those are some weak tactics.

56
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:34,760
What?

57
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,340
Defenders! Keep on doing what you're doing. Don't slack off.

58
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:43,600
I think we held out pretty well during the first half. Aoi screwed up some, but overall,

59
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:49,500
he's improving. As long as we keep going and don't give up, we win. So let's go take it all!

60
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:50,240
Yeah!

61
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:55,360
Ashito!

62
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:56,220
Huh?

63
00:04:56,780 --> 00:05:03,320
I'm going on the attack. Trust me. Relying on Yoshitsune to win isn't gonna help us out in the long run.

64
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:09,640
What are you gonna do? What are you gonna do? I know you're itching. You miss scoring the goals.

65
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:22,120
Changing it up, are we? They're trying to make it harder for us to get the ball to Yoshitsune at all.

66
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:28,880
Don't be like me. You're following the path you're supposed to all on your own.

67
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:37,060
Yeah, but... What if I don't like the path I'm supposed to be on? I want yours! I want to attack!

68
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:43,360
And now that they're swarming Yoshitsune, there are more open spaces! I could actually score!

69
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:48,540
Something tells me I might be about to grasp onto something great.

70
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:53,540
Fukuda, he... he speaks highly of you. To the A-team. You know?

71
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:58,040
I can always go back to the way I was.

72
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:04,320
The right wing's open! Head for the space!

73
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:07,000
There he goes. Tokushi's moving up.

74
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:11,680
What's with the space on the right wing? It looks different for some reason.

75
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:18,560
You okay, Ishiki? He's still feeling that injury from the first half.

76
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:20,680
I'm not gonna let them pass me!

77
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:24,520
Tokushi? He's gonna catch up at that speed!

78
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:31,560
If Takashima and I sandwich this guy, we can stop him right there so he can have it!

79
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:51,400
Huh? Did those defenders just run from the ball?

80
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:56,540
What the heck was that crap about?

81
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,960
You need to communicate with each other!

82
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:02,260
It's not that hard! All you had to do was talk to each other!

83
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:05,180
And just now, you both made a choice not to do that!

84
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:07,000
We're all playing defense today!

85
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:10,400
We have to win, and I don't care who does it or how!

86
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:15,780
Tsukushima, we gotta make some changes to the system.

87
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:21,700
Togashi, I'm gonna need to talk to you after the game.

88
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:26,180
Just make a note that from now on, we're gonna give this win all we got!

89
00:07:26,540 --> 00:07:26,780
Huh?

90
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:29,680
What the heck is going on with those guys?

91
00:07:29,980 --> 00:07:32,320
I cannot believe they made such a stupid mistake!

92
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:36,020
The second half just started, and the momentum's not on our side at all.

93
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:40,240
I bet they're gonna pull Ishiki from the game.

94
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:44,880
That was Asperion's number nine we just saw leaving on a stretcher.

95
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:46,620
What a time for a new player to come on.

96
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:48,820
Hey, Shimizu!

97
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:51,220
Togashi!

98
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:53,500
What the...

99
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:54,940
Aoi!

100
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:59,340
Got that?

101
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:16,660
Just one more goal for the comeback!

102
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,020
Remember, stay tight on Yoshitsune!

103
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:20,020
Yeah!

104
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:24,780
Conceding due to a defensive error, and after a change at center-back,

105
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:27,580
Isperion's defense sure seems to be falling apart!

106
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:31,660
All we gotta do is press hard and snatch that ball away!

107
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:33,980
Wait a minute, something's different!

108
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:37,400
I see, they've changed their entire system on us!

109
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:41,920
Ishiki's replacement will be Numizu.

110
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:43,800
I'll keep him at center-back.

111
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:48,020
Shimizu, the anchorman, will drop back into the defensive line.

112
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:50,000
And both fullbacks?

113
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,160
Go upfield.

114
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:55,640
Both you and Togashi are supposed to fly forward.

115
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:57,000
That's from Coach Nozomi.

116
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,740
You're still a fullback, though, alright?

117
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:02,200
So don't forget to defend, okay?

118
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:03,700
Keep that in mind up there.

119
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:05,800
Oh, and...

120
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,220
Coach wanted me to give you a message.

121
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:09,940
He said to tell you,

122
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:12,960
Attacking from defense isn't a whole new ballgame.

123
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:16,260
Take what you've learned and apply it to attacking.

124
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:17,080
That's it.

125
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:21,660
I can go upfield?

126
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:29,540
I'm allowed to move upfield and score?

127
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,480
That makes me unbelievably happy!

128
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:39,120
I'm frickin' stoked!

129
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,780
But is it really that simple?

130
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:45,180
Whenever I want, while still playing defense?

131
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:49,760
How do I attack, while still maintaining the back line?

132
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:54,180
I want to go upfield right now, but...

133
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:55,260
Damn it!

134
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:57,160
I don't know what I should be doing!

135
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,000
Ashito!

136
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,500
Hurry up! Let's go!

137
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,720
Stick with me! I could use your support!

138
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:09,100
Cover the spaces on the right for me, but not too close, okay?

139
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:10,600
That's a great idea!

140
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:11,600
Let's go!

141
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:21,840
Yoshitsune's open!

142
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:22,700
Ugh!

143
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:31,260
We fully expected for this game to be tied,

144
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:33,700
but we had to move the timing up.

145
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:39,700
Ishiki's injury stopped the game, but we had always planned to alter the formation at this point in the match.

146
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:44,700
So now, we wait for the players to figure it all out? That right?

147
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:49,700
Let's hope they've all learned something out there.

148
00:10:53,700 --> 00:10:56,700
What the... Why can't I get the ball?!

149
00:10:56,700 --> 00:11:05,700
I know this feeling. I've been here. It's exactly like the Seikyo High match.

150
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:09,700
A triangle!

151
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:16,700
What?

152
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:19,700
Don't just stand there, go get the ball!

153
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:26,700
Yeah, right. Good luck trying, you dweebs. The only difference between then and now is I'm in Asuri's position.

154
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:31,700
Take what you've learned on defense and apply it to attacking.

155
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:34,700
Their number 19's closing in.

156
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:37,700
Hurry! Here, Ultimo! Pass it back!

157
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:41,700
Yoshitsune!

158
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:56,700
Otimo, I'm trusting you to know how my mind works. Please try to read me. Here it comes!

159
00:11:57,700 --> 00:12:01,700
Do you want to pass? Okay. But where?

160
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:03,700
I see it!

161
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:07,700
I'm in the back. And that gives me an advantage.

162
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:13,700
I can be the eyes for the players in front of me. I'll give them instructions and tell them what they can't see.

163
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:16,700
I'll tell them exactly how to score like I would!

164
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:24,700
Watching you enjoy yourself like this makes me very happy too.

165
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:27,700
The pass got through?

166
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:28,700
Hey, Ultimo!

167
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,700
He's open in prime position!

168
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:32,700
I can shoot!

169
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:33,700
Don't shoot!

170
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:40,700
That was close. I didn't see him coming. But thanks to that, it looked like a fake out.

171
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:43,700
Shoot!

172
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:44,700
Now!

173
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:48,700
It's clear!

174
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:59,700
I'm just one player out of eleven. I'm a little bit jealous of you too.

175
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:03,700
Everyone's one player out of eleven in a game of soccer.

176
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:07,700
That was weird. What did he mean by that?

177
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:22,700
I have a direct shot at the goal from here. Just like in the Seikyo High match. I'm farther away than I was then. But the shot's still on.

178
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:31,700
Huh? Tachibana's completely open. And he's in the perfect spot. Rather than going for the tough shot, I should pass to him.

179
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:39,700
No, wait. If I nudge it a little to the right, I can avoid the crowd. And take the shot! That's what I'll do.

180
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:44,700
Come up with four viable options. And out of those four...

181
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:46,700
I choose.

182
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:48,700
I choose.

183
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:49,700
I choose.

184
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:51,700
Ugh!

185
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:52,700
Ugh!

186
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:53,700
Ugh!

187
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:54,700
Ugh!

188
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:55,700
Ugh!

189
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:56,540
Eww!

190
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:57,360
Ah!

191
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:06,840
Ah, we did it!

192
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:08,420
Togashi, let's go!

193
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:11,640
A fullback providing the assist to another fullback?

194
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:13,560
There's something you don't see every day.

195
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:15,920
Huh?

196
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:18,280
Togashi!

197
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:20,400
You are the best!

198
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:21,920
The ball came in from behind you,

199
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,620
but that didn't matter to this beast!

200
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:25,720
You just went flying up high with that header!

201
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:26,520
Man!

202
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:29,720
Look at you, scoring despite being a fullback!

203
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:30,760
Hey, Ashito!

204
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,500
That was a baller assist!

205
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:39,640
It was the only option.

206
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:42,800
If we were gonna score, we needed Togashi's height.

207
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:44,800
Hey, Ashito.

208
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,140
That was a great assist.

209
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:49,340
Thanks, but what happened to you?

210
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:50,420
You spaced out.

211
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:53,560
You were just standing there.

212
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:56,220
And you were offside.

213
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,660
It's happening again.

214
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:03,100
That look.

215
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:06,040
Sweet, and yet fragile.

216
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:07,380
When it comes to soccer,

217
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:08,980
you really don't know much, do you?

218
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:14,180
Yep, it's a world I just don't understand.

219
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:19,080
Oh, hang on.

220
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,520
Are you leaving?

221
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:22,280
I just remembered.

222
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,920
I have something for you.

223
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,160
Your photo.

224
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:26,000
Photo?

225
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,160
From the last game.

226
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,700
I sure got some fun ones.

227
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,360
Sorry for not asking for permission.

228
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:32,440
It's a thank you for showing me around.

229
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:35,000
There are two copies.

230
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,200
Give one to Aoi for me, all right?

231
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,500
Thank you!

232
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:47,680
What's the deal with that kid?

233
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:51,580
I don't know what it is that triggers him,

234
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:53,920
but it's like he becomes someone else.

235
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,920
Improvements always welcome,

236
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:58,220
but from a coach's standpoint,

237
00:15:58,220 --> 00:16:01,160
how far out can you even predict when instructing him?

238
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:04,220
Nozomi?

239
00:16:04,220 --> 00:16:11,500
I don't think predictions are possible here, Tsukishima.

240
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:14,500
Fukuda?

241
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:18,000
You ever been able to predict anything in youth soccer?

242
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,340
Yeah, right.

243
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:22,000
We're going into stoppage time!

244
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,400
Hold the lead, you guys!

245
00:16:34,220 --> 00:16:35,960
Just a little longer!

246
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:37,160
You can do it!

247
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:51,000
HELP NOOOOOOO!

248
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,500
He held on!

249
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:56,500
Yes!

250
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:58,580
Let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go.

251
00:17:04,220 --> 00:17:12,500
In the end, my last contribution in this game was the assist, the one for Tokushi's goalie.

252
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:28,040
You had a good assist toward the end there, but after that the balance was totally off.

253
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:34,320
You racked up miles in the attack, switching from offense to defense over and over again.

254
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:37,320
It's like you deliberately wore yourself out.

255
00:17:37,320 --> 00:17:38,320
You're right.

256
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:43,960
After that assist, my mind started to get hazy.

257
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:49,460
I don't remember what I did right after, much less what happened the rest of the game.

258
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:55,140
I heard you were killing it on defense, Ashiton.

259
00:17:56,340 --> 00:18:00,740
Nozomi was raving about how you were barking orders effectively, eliminating spaces.

260
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:03,700
Defense isn't easy.

261
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:08,180
There are a lot more structural rules than playing on offense.

262
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:11,220
It takes some hardcore skill to verbalize moves.

263
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:15,220
But if you're able to shout instructions like you just did,

264
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:17,460
it means you're able to put those thoughts into words.

265
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:21,700
You applied that to your attack, and it got you an assist.

266
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:23,860
I am impressed.

267
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:24,740
Great job.

268
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:31,300
Fukuda, he speaks highly of you, to the A-team, you know?

269
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:35,220
So, uh, help me understand something.

270
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,180
Why didn't you take the shot?

271
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:46,980
I'm not looking for the right answer, trying to get all judgy about it.

272
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:53,860
It's just, we won the game and yet it looks an awful lot like you're over here sulking.

273
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:58,180
It's because I suck.

274
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:02,900
I'm not only frustrated because I couldn't play consistently for a full 90 minutes,

275
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:05,780
but I want to be a forward again.

276
00:19:06,740 --> 00:19:10,900
And yet when I was in that moment, I chose to pass instead of scoring.

277
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:13,700
I have no idea why I did that.

278
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:15,380
It worked out for you.

279
00:19:15,380 --> 00:19:17,380
Me not taking shots, didn't it?

280
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:21,620
You branded me as a failed forward and that backs you up.

281
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:25,220
Quit doubting yourself as a player.

282
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:27,940
That's the only criticism I'd make.

283
00:19:28,820 --> 00:19:30,820
I wonder why I doubt myself.

284
00:19:31,620 --> 00:19:34,820
Your next opponent is Tokyo Musashino, right?

285
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:35,780
I've seen videos.

286
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,820
They are one hell of a team, you know?

287
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:40,900
I don't think you're ready for them yet.

288
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:47,460
But, depending on how well you do in that match, I might consider moving you to the A-Team.

289
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:49,060
Good luck.

290
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:55,220
Ashita!

291
00:19:55,220 --> 00:19:58,340
No! We finally won a game!

292
00:19:58,340 --> 00:20:01,060
And it was all thanks to that assist of yours!

293
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:03,780
Yeah, and you did really well on defense, Aoi!

294
00:20:03,780 --> 00:20:04,340
Thank you!

295
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:05,540
Get off!

296
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:06,340
Yo, Aoi!

297
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:10,020
Hey, Ishiki! How's your leg?

298
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:14,740
Don't worry about me. We won. That's all that really matters.

299
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:19,860
Ow!

300
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:21,780
Thanks, bro!

301
00:20:25,220 --> 00:20:25,780
Hmm.

302
00:20:39,060 --> 00:20:40,580
How about it, Hana?

303
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:43,300
That was the first game I played in quite a while!

304
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:45,860
I'd say you picked a good day to show up, wouldn't you?

305
00:20:49,460 --> 00:20:50,980
You were incredible out there!

306
00:20:51,620 --> 00:20:54,340
Well, I had to be. I knew you were gonna be in the stands.

307
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:54,740
Huh?

308
00:20:54,740 --> 00:20:57,460
I reserved my premium shiz for the fans, you know.

309
00:20:58,500 --> 00:20:59,860
But you did show up late!

310
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:02,660
Next time, make it for the kickoff!

311
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:03,780
I'm counting on ya!

312
00:21:05,300 --> 00:21:06,420
Hey there, Aoi!

313
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:08,660
I'm Aoi Kaneko from Soccer Every.

314
00:21:08,660 --> 00:21:10,900
Do you have a minute to talk to me about the game today?

315
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:11,620
What's going on?

316
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:13,220
At least that's what I wanted to say.

317
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:15,940
But I'm kind of late for another interview.

318
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,940
It's a different Metro League matchup.

319
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:19,700
But please, let me leave you my card.

320
00:21:20,340 --> 00:21:21,700
Let's get together sometime.

321
00:21:22,660 --> 00:21:24,580
Now, wait just a minute there, kid.

322
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:27,860
Are you trying to contact a player without going through the proper channels?

323
00:21:28,580 --> 00:21:30,260
There's another Metro League match?

324
00:21:30,260 --> 00:21:34,420
Yeah, it's, uh, the Tokyo Musashino Youth match.

325
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:35,940
Musashino Youth?

326
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:38,980
Uh-huh, there's sudden improvements got everyone talking.

327
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:39,780
Ashito!

328
00:21:39,780 --> 00:21:40,260
Oh?

329
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:42,660
Uh, what is it, Otomo?

330
00:21:43,380 --> 00:21:44,900
Ashito, we have a problem.

331
00:21:45,460 --> 00:21:45,700
Huh?

332
00:21:48,420 --> 00:21:49,060
Got a minute?

333
00:21:50,260 --> 00:21:50,900
Sure, why?

334
00:21:53,860 --> 00:21:54,820
In the next match...

335
00:21:56,660 --> 00:21:58,580
I, uh, I don't want you to play me.

336
00:22:01,220 --> 00:22:02,500
My confidence is shut.

337
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:08,820
He doesn't want to play at all?

338
00:22:09,380 --> 00:22:11,380
Tachibana actually said that.

339
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:11,940
Yeah, man.

340
00:22:13,140 --> 00:22:15,380
It's because he'd have to play against his old team.

341
00:22:16,340 --> 00:22:17,460
Tokyo Musashino.

342
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:22,980
Otomo, let's go watch their game today.

343
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:23,300
What?

344
00:22:25,620 --> 00:22:26,980
We'll take Tachibana too.

345
00:22:29,380 --> 00:22:31,780
It'll be good for us to know what kind of game they play.

346
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:34,580
Let's see what they're made of.

347
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,286
Next time on Awashi, what we lack.

